*Reaper wears bandoliers of grenade shells.<ref name="ArtofOverwatch">''[[The Art of Overwatch]]''</ref>
*According to Reaper's dog tag on his Soldier: 24 skin, his blood type is AB Negative, his soldier ID number is 06 0000 0024, and he has no religion.
*Reaper was a big basketball and football fan.<ref>2017-04-17, [https://twitter.com/westofhouse/status/854198483892305920 Michael Chu's Twitter]. ''Twitter'', accessed on 2018-10-17</ref> His favorite team was the L.A Lakers.<ref>2017-03-30, [https://twitter.com/westofhouse/status/847585096332787712 Michael Chu's Twitter]. ''Twitter'', accessed on 2018-10-17</ref>
*Reaper is of Latino descent.<ref>2019-11-03, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2OTcKgGcCBU BlizzCon 2019 Q&A]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2020-01-20</ref>  
*His Mariachi skin might imply that he is of Mexican ancestry.
*As Reaper, Reyes has apparently spent much of his time stalking Martina.<ref name = "ReaperQuotes">''[[Overwatch 2]]'', ''[[Reaper/Quotes|Reaper Quotes]]''</ref>
*Reaper dislikes [[Oasis]].<ref name = "ReaperQuotes"/>

====Disputed Information====
*Contradictory information exists as to the nature of Reaper and Morrison's relationship. An [[Atlas News]] post in 2015 stated that Morrison becoming head of Overwatch was the source of the rift between them.<ref name = "FadingGlory">2015-07-07, [http://us.battle.net/overwatch/en/blog/19809396/ Fading Glory: On the Trail of Jack Morrison]. ''Blizzard Entertainment'', accessed on 2015-07-07</ref>  In 2018, [[Jeff Kaplan]] stated that there was no rift, that Reyes was happy for Morrison to have the more political role and be "number two," as there would be less accountability.<ref name = "KaplanReaper">January, 2018, [https://www.reddit.com/r/Overwatch/comments/7bs5z4/jeff_kaplan_on_morrison_and_reyes/ Jeff Kaplan on Morrison and Reyes]. ''Reddit'', accessed on 2018-02-08</ref>
*At some point after Null Sector's return, Reaper and his fellow Talon members engaged Overwatch in a firefight at [[Petra]]. Talon was forced to retreat.<ref name = "VentureNew">2024-03-28, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JF6tLqe_FSA Venture | New Hero Gameplay Trailer | Overwatch 2]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2024-03-28</ref>

===Cultural References===
*Reaper bears resemblance to the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_%28personification%29 Grim Reaper], from various real-world cultures.
*Reaper's reload animation is possibly a reference to the lobby shootout scene from ''The Matrix''.
*Reaper's legendary ''Cursed Captain'' skin is a possible nod to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walt_Disney_Company Disney]'s rendition of [https://pirates.fandom.com/wiki/Davy_Jones Davy Jones]. The main Antagonist of the 2006 film [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pirates_of_the_Caribbean:_Dead_Man%27s_Chest Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man's Chest].
*Death Blossom might be a reference to 
**a weapon used in the 1984 movie ''The Last Starfighter'' named Death Blossom.
**Katarina from League of Legends, whose ultimate "Death Lotus" behaves similarly.
**Strafe, an ability for the Demon Hunter class from Diablo III'','' another Blizzard title.
**the art of Gun-kata from the movie Equilibrium.
**a military term used to describe a group of men firing wildly in all directions surrounding the group.
*The "CRW-ND" written on Plague Doctor and Nevermore skins' guns might be a reference to "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xO7NB46hvsI crowning]", a technique from the game Left 4 Dead that involves focusing the devastating fire of a shotgun in point blank range on the Witch, a very high health enemy, essentially killing her before she can react - this being a reference to Reaper's tank busting abilities.
**It may be a play on the gaming term "owned", crossed with the skins' "crow" theme ("crow-ned", rather than "crown-ed").

====In Other Blizzard Games====
*[http://starcraft.wikia.com/wiki/Reaper Reapers] are a type of unit in [[Blizzard Entertainment]]'s ''StarCraft'' series. Like Reaper himself, they dual-wield firearms and wear masks.
*A Reaper portrait is available in ''[http://starcraft.wikia.com/wiki/StarCraft_II StarCraft II]'' for those who purchase the ''[[Origins Edition]]''.<ref>2015-11-06, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/overwatch-origins-edition-pre-orders-have-begun Overwatch: Origins Edition (PC) Pre-Orders have Begun]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2015-11-07</ref>
*Reaper's stance bears resemblance to the ''Diablo III'' antagonist Malthael.
*Reaper appears as a cosplay skin for Valla in ''[[Heroes of the Storm]]''.

===Merchandise===
*A Funko Pop Reaper figurine was released in June, 2016.<ref>2016-02-26, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/pre-order-funko-overwatch-pop-vinyl-figures Pre-Order FUNKO Overwatch POP Vinyl Figures]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2016-03-11</ref>
*A 12" Reaper statue was made available in 2017.<ref>2016-11-26, [http://www.polygon.com/2016/11/26/13752638/overwatch-reaper-statue-premium Overwatch’s newest premium collectible is a badass Reaper statue]. ''Polygon'', accessed on 2016-11-28</ref>
*A Figma Reaper statue became available in 2019.<ref>[https://gear.blizzard.com/us/figma-reaper Figma Reaper], ''Blizzard Store''. Accessed on 2018-05-17</ref>

===Development===
[[File:ReaperTitan.jpg|200px|left|thumb|The Reaper class from Project Titan]]
[[File:Reaperearlyart.jpg|thumb|Reaper early concept art]]
Prior to the development of ''Overwatch'', Reaper was the name of one of the player classes in the cancelled [[Project Titan]], which in the original pitch for the game that would become ''Overwatch'' was envisioned as wielding dual shotguns and a magnum, and using the abilities Death Blossom and Shadow Walk.<ref>Blizzcon 2017, Overwatch: Archives</ref> This class was reworked into the present day Reaper as one of the first three characters designed for ''Overwatch'', alongside Tracer and Widowmaker.<ref>2016-04-22, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bTMnJ5XJH6Q The Story of Overwatch: Return of the 90s Shooter]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2016-09-08</ref> The character of Reaper was inspired entirely by concept art for the game&mdash;his actual character was developed after his appearance was presented.<ref name = "Origins">2015-05-27, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/blizzcon-2014-overwatch-origins-panel-transcript/3 BlizzCon 2014 – Overwatch Origins Panel Transcript]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2015-05-30</ref> Originally, he only had a single shotgun.<ref>''[[Forging Worlds: Stories Behind the Art of Blizzard Entertainment]]''</ref>

Under ''Overwatch'''s original leveling system, Reaper's wraith form would give him healing abilities once he reached a certain level.<ref>2015-12-19, [http://www.polygon.com/2015/12/16/10323334/overwatch-blizzard-progression-system Overwatch's two failed progression systems explained]. ''Polygon'', accessed on 2015-12-19</ref> Reaper once had a slimmer design with a mask that was more human looking and dual wielded SMGs.<ref name="ArtofOverwatch"/>

[[File:Overwatch2Reaper.jpeg|thumb|Overwatch 2 Reaper early concept art]]
Along with most heroes, Reaper's appearance was redesigned for ''[[Overwatch 2]]''. They spoke about integrating his armour, cloak and iconic cowl into his new look, while keeping the classic reaper silhouette. They experimented with his colour scheme in development, such as trying completely silver arms and more jacket layers. Ultimately, they replaced his "bone white" mask and other features with a more "deadly, edgy silver" to change his colour scheme. <ref name = "Overwatch2BehindScenes">2021-02-20, [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lRj-GotnNaQ BlizzConline 2021 | Behind the Scenes of Overwatch 2 | Overwatch]. ''YouTube'', accessed on 2021-03-13</ref>.

